{
 "answer": "Authority and independence are separate axes. PRIMARY is the thing itself (RFC/PEP/schema/license/implementing source); MAINTAINER is official docs; PRACTITIONER is first-hand observation; RETELLER restates without adding observation. Independence fail-closes to SYNDICATED on verbatim copies. Two mechanically independent raters (A publisher-class / URL+exact-sha256; B content-ngram / body markers + 5-gram Jaccard; URL sealed) scored a committed 40-source set. Cohen kappa authority=0.832775919732 (agree=35/40 disagree=5); independence=0.718969555035 (agree=34/40 disagree=6); joint=0.700598802395. Authority disagreements concentrate on {'MAINTAINER|PRACTITIONER': 1, 'MAINTAINER|PRIMARY': 1, 'MAINTAINER|RETELLER': 1, 'RETELLER|MAINTAINER': 1, 'RETELLER|PRACTITIONER': 1}. Independence disagreements concentrate on {'PARALLEL|ORIGINATING': 4, 'DERIVED|ORIGINATING': 1, 'ORIGINATING|DERIVED': 1}. PARALLEL is A-only (URL topic peers) while B maps those rows to ORIGINATING unless measurement-voice n-grams overlap; a near-copy of hashlib docs (Jaccard 0.88) is DERIVED for B and also pulls the original docs into DERIVED because n-gram overlap is symmetric. Five verbatim syndicated GIL roundups (S01-S05) score SYNDICATED on both raters; the unique-URL poller scores all five ORIGINATING, so the independence axis is not 'has a URL'. Raters are disjoint-feature mechanical implementations (local-parallel analog of different vendors), not a second LLM on the same prompt. SUCCESS:RES-0144",
